# Shared workflow guardrails

## Applicability

The full Plan TODO workflow applies only when:

- the Agent is executing a TODO from an accepted or current plan; or
- the user explicitly requests the Plan TODO, one-task-one-branch, or equivalent workflow.

Ordinary edits, read-only investigation, explanations, and ad-hoc maintenance do not start this workflow.

## Decision gate

Stop and ask before proceeding when a product, architecture, scope, dependency, data, security, deployment, review, or Git decision can change implementation direction or history. Do not silently choose a consequential default.

## Human approval gate

When a TODO is marked `[需人工验收]`, `human approval required`, or equivalent:

- implementation, local verification, and an implementation commit may be completed first;
- then stop, preserve the branch state, report changes, verification, and remaining risk;
- do not mark the plan TODO complete, write its final report, push, open or merge a PR, or delete the branch until the user explicitly replies `approve`, `Approved`, `通过`, or an equally clear acceptance phrase.

Without an explicit approval marker, follow the accepted plan's stated completion gates.

## Git safety

- Use one task branch per Plan TODO; do not execute Plan TODO work directly on `main` or `master`.
- Never revert unrelated user changes.
- Never use `git reset --hard`, `git checkout -- <path>`, force-push, or destructive cleanup unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Never bypass hooks, checks, required reviews, or branch protection.
- Do not amend unless the user explicitly requests it and the target commit is local and safe to rewrite.
- Do not commit, push, open a PR, or merge unless the user has explicitly authorized that operation.